## 1. Breakdown of Built Components

The package is organized into two distinct layers adhering strictly to all requirements (no JSX, no `as any`, modular D3 imports, AA contrast, WCAG/axe compliance, typed end-to-end):

### Layer 1: Core (Framework-Free D3 Engine)
Located in [`src/core/`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/core/):
- **[`timeSeries`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/core/timeSeries.ts)**:
  - Multi-series line, area, and stacked area rendering.
  - Multi-axis support (left and optional right y-axis).
  - Time x-axis with automatic tick sizing across viewports.
  - Shaded horizontal threshold lines with status labels and vertical incident/event bands.
  - Gap detection: breaks paths across `null` points or time intervals exceeding `gapAfter` without false interpolation.
  - Live stream mode: `append()` slides window smoothly; updates batched via `requestAnimationFrame`.
  - LTTB decimation: automatically downsamples dense datasets exceeding pixel resolution.
  - Interactions: Pointer Events for drag panning, pinch zoom, `touch-action: pan-y` (preserving vertical page scroll), wheel zooming only when `Ctrl`/`Cmd` is held, click-to-resume Live tracking button.
  - Full keyboard navigation (arrow keys move crosshair point-by-point, `+`/`-` zoom, `0` resets, `Escape` hides tooltip).
  - Dual visual encoding: dash patterns differentiate lines when $>4$ series are rendered.
  - Screen reader accessible visually hidden table representation (`table: true`).
- **[`sparkline`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/core/sparkline.ts)**: Tiny inline trendline for stat tiles and list rows with zero axes, last value dot, and optional min/max extent markers.
- **[`bars`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/core/bars.ts)**: Grouped and stacked bar charts in horizontal and vertical orientations with interactive hover tooltips and series toggles.
- **[`meter`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/core/meter.ts)**: Linear capacity gauge with warn/bad thresholds, full ARIA meter semantics (`role="meter"`, `aria-valuenow`, `aria-valuemin`, `aria-valuemax`, `aria-valuetext`), and explicit text status ("Normal", "Warning", "Critical").
- **[`heatmap`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/core/heatmap.ts)**: 2D density matrix with time on the x-axis and bucket categories on the y-axis (optimized for latency distributions) with continuous color scales.
- **[`stateTimeline`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/core/stateTimeline.ts)**: Discrete status spans over time per row (e.g. pod phases: Pending/Running/Failed; volume copy modes: RW/WO/ERR) with interactive tooltips and accessible summary table.

### Adapters & Utilities
- **[`fromPromMatrix`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/adapters.ts)**: Transforms VictoriaMetrics/Prometheus `query_range` matrix responses into `Series[]`, converting seconds to milliseconds, handling `NaN`, `+Inf`, `-Inf`, and extracting labels.
- **[`fromPromVector`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/adapters.ts)**: Transforms Prometheus instant vector queries into structured data.
- **[`lttb`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/lttb.ts)**: Largest-Triangle-Three-Buckets downsampling algorithm.
- **[`formatUnit`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/units.ts)**: Unified metric formatting engine supporting bytes (IEC binary units: KiB, MiB, GiB, TiB), bytes/s, percentage (%), seconds/duration, and counts with SI prefixes.

### Layer 2: The Mesh-Web Bridge
Located in [`src/bridge.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/bridge.ts):
- `TimeSeriesChart`, `SparklineChart`, `BarsChart`, `MeterChart`, `HeatmapChart`, and `StateTimelineChart`.
- Declares `needs('dom')` and mounts onto `cx.dom.surface`.
- Avoids THE TRAP: signal subscriptions are isolated within `this.cx.effect(...)` inside the component body, preventing host element re-creation and preserving the SVG, D3 state, and DOM event listeners across signal updates.

### Design System & Accessibility
Located in [`src/charts.css`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/src/charts.css):
- Uses CSS custom properties with `light-dark()` matching `mesh-web-kit`'s tokens.
- Fully audited with `axe-core` in both light and dark modes with **0 violations**.
- Responsive down to 320 px mobile frame with minimum 44x44px touch targets.

### Interactive Gallery App
Located in [`examples/gallery/`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/examples/gallery/):
- Fully-featured interactive demo application mounting all 6 charts with simulated VictoriaMetrics streams and a 320 px mobile frame toggle.

