## 5. Report & Feedback

The detailed report has been written to [`agent-runs/results/01-charts-kit.md`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh/mesh-web-charts/agent-runs/results/01-charts-kit.md).

### Feedback on `mesh-web` / `mesh-web-kit`:
1. **`cx.dom.surface` and Reactive Isolation**: `surface()` is a very clean escape hatch for D3. However, developers must take special care to separate the surface node creation from signal reads to avoid re-triggering the surface factory function on signal changes. Providing a documented helper pattern (or adding a section in `app-model.md`) would help future authors building WebGL/Canvas/SVG integrations.
2. **Component Vocabulary Clarity**: `mesh-web`'s DOM driver requires abstract primitives (`Stack`, `Row`, `Heading`, `Text`, `Button`, `Card`, `Grid`) rather than HTML tags (`div`, `header`, etc.). A friendly error message suggesting the equivalent primitive would improve developer onboarding.

